            "url": "https://github.com/ZZZZihan/anxin-work-rights/pull/45#discussion_r4308160120",
            "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject coordinated surnames outside the finite list**\n\nWhen two workers are identified by single surnames and the second surname is absent from `commonSurname`, this branch treats the coordinated subject as one person. For example, `王和欧2026年1月全部应付工资合计4000元` with model-supplied subject `王和欧` and `scope: \"individual\"` receives no review issue and exposes `4000.00` as an eligible complete individual total, while `王和赵` is correctly blocked. Do not use an incomplete surname list to prove that an embedded conjunction belongs to a personal name; unknown one-character pairs should remain collective or unresolved.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->"
          }
        ]
      }
